--- !u!114 &8258527270560430681
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5895071840021699718}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 131601e0e83c24d4494c0aaf7c441c5e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Dialogue
  DialogueBox: {fileID: 6200309184073947706}
  DialogueText: {fileID: 8407287007781049157}
  NextLinePrompt: {fileID: 8759157761375450446}
  SpeakerText: {fileID: 7968335808194118951}
  ChoiceButton1: {fileID: 7094657776742189753}
  ChoiceButton2: {fileID: 2601269925529262852}
  ChoiceButton1Text: {fileID: 814046364647351370}
  ChoiceButton2Text: {fileID: 3967013956273380826}
  DialogueSessions:
  - SessionName: Welcome
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Oh! You must be the new assistant designer!
      Choices:
      - ButtonText: Yup, that's me!
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: Good, we're going to need that enthusiasm, there will be much work
            to do.
          Choices: []
      - ButtonText: What are you talking about?
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: You know, the application that you sent in? the onboarding email
            we sent? In case you didn't know already, you got the job.
          Choices:
          - ButtonText: Of course, how could I forget!
            Lines:
            - Speaker: Dennis
              Text: I was beginning to think I had the wrong person, but it seems
                you're just forgetful. Try not to do that on the job.
              Choices: []
          - ButtonText: Doesn't ring a bell.
            Lines:
            - Speaker: Dennis
              Text: Well, you're here now so, congratulations, you're the new assistant
                costume designer!
              Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: I'm Dennis the costume designer, and welcome to our very... lively costume
        shop. It's a charming place, really.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: However old it may be, the theater needs your help!
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: The theater is going out of business, and they only have enough money
        to put on one last show. If this show doesn't sell out, then it's done for.
      Choices:
      - ButtonText: Oh no! That's terrible!
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: Terrible indeed. It *is* really old, and it is literally falling
            apart, and it *would* be a lot easier to just- you know what? Never mind.
          Choices: []
      - ButtonText: How do I even fix that?
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: You were hired for a reason. Don't tell me you didn't read the job
            description.
          Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Unfortunately for us, every shop employee was "let go" due to budget
        cuts, so you have to pick up the slack.
      Choices:
      - ButtonText: Put me in coach!
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: Wow, you really are eager. Click on the arrow above to head to the
            costume shop and I'll show you around.
          Choices: []
      - ButtonText: Why can't you just do it?
        Lines:
        - Speaker: Dennis
          Text: I- uh, I'm the designer. The company doesn't allow the designer to
            work in the costume shop. Yeah, that sounds right... How about we start
            the tour? Click on the arrow above to head to the shop.
          Choices: []
  - SessionName: Shop tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is the costume shop, where all the magic happens. Well, if you could
        even call it "magic".
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'It''s more like... motivation only by the threat of your job being taken
        if you don''t finish in time, and the whole entire town will look down upon
        you and the entire theater if you mess up. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'Like I said, magic. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is the main shop area. This is where you will find the entrance
        to every room.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'Currently, you can access the storage room, the desk, the sewing table,
        and the meeting room. Don''t ask about the compiling room, it''s infested
        with rats right now, so best not to go in there right now. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Anyways, feel free to take a look around the place, and I'll be right
        behind you to explain. Don't worry about the time for now, just explore and
        we'll get started on the show after 6 weeks.
      Choices: []
  - SessionName: Sewing tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is our sewing table where all the sewing happens.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'Here you pick the piece, like top or bottom, a type, like sweater or
        t-shirt, and a style like futuristic or 1960''s. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'Then you pick a fabric from the fabric list which determines the material
        and color. The grade of the final result is determined by how well you do
        in the minigame. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'Oh, and we don''t know exactly how the craft person works, or who they
        are, but we do know that if we sew something for them, they will return shoes
        and hats for us. So for shoes and hats, just keep doing what you do for other
        patterns. '
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: 'That''s it for the sewing table, go check out the other rooms if you
        haven''t already. '
      Choices: []
  - SessionName: Storage tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is the storage room. You can take clothing hangers from your personal
        rack and onto the storage rack.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: You can also sort by different factors, like color, type, and piece.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Any orders online also show up here.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Make sure to go check out the other rooms if you haven't already.
      Choices: []
  - SessionName: Desk tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is your very own desk, just for you! Here is where your computer
        and calendar is.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Here on slamazon is where you buy fabric for sewing, or full clothing
        pieces.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Shipping isn't fast, however. Clothing takes time to arrive, so make
        sure to keep your eye on the date as well as the calendar. When the week
        arrives, make sure to check your storage for the clothing piece you ordered.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: The options available to buy change every week, so stop by often to buy
        things before they reset.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Also watch your total budget up in the top left. You currently have $600,
        but that can run out pretty quickly when buying for an actual show.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Go check out the other available rooms if you haven't already.
      Choices: []
  - SessionName: Meeting tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: This is the meeting room where you meet with me and the director during
        an actual show.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Here we plan and debrief you on how many actors are in the show, what
        colors we need, the basis of the show, and what styles we need.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: We aren't starting production on this show for another 6 weeks, so don't
        worry too much about what we have written down here, but let it inspire you
        as you mess around in the costume shop.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Make sure to check out the other rooms if you haven't already.
      Choices: []
  - SessionName: End tutorial
    Lines:
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Looks like this is the end of your tour.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Feel free to continue looking around and gathering costumes for the rest
        of the 6 weeks.
      Choices: []
    - Speaker: Dennis
      Text: Good luck, you're going to need the practice!
      Choices: []
  TypeSpeed: 0.03
